    "sectionDescriptions": {
      "decisionCriteria": "Author the rules the resolution gate enforces (and the DNA-Coefficient measures divergence against). Each criterion is a reusable <strong>Compliance Check</strong>.",
      "evidenceSources": "Bind the past decisions the DNA-Coefficient is measured against. Add one or more sources — a <strong>Delta table</strong>, a <strong>Data Product</strong>, or an <strong>Asset</strong> (volume file, table, or view). Each maps its columns to the canonical AR elements via the column map.",
      "participants": "The N-functional gate and review. <strong>Approvers</strong> count toward the affirmation gate. <strong> Reviewers</strong> are interviewed during the review process to confirm the relation reflects reality. A principal can be both.",
      "requires": "Prerequisite ARs: each must resolve <strong>approved</strong> before this one decides. Keyed by the family slug (not the version) so this AR keeps working when a prerequisite is version-bumped. Save requires this AR to carry a slug of its own.",
      "resourceRefs": "Where field values come from. Instead of a plain literal, back a canonical field (<code>actor_identity</code>, <code>object_id</code>, <code>domain_context.{{keyPlaceholder}}</code>) with a typed pointer. An <strong> Ontos entity</strong> ref re-resolves against the knowledge graph at eval time so the value stays current when the underlying concept, product, or domain changes. <strong> MCP tool</strong> refs call a Unity Catalog MCP service at decision time; criteria can compare against the resolved value as <code>obj.ref_{{fieldPlaceholder}}</code> (dots become underscores, e.g. <code>obj.ref_actor_identity</code>).",
      "dnaSchedule": "How often the DNA-Coefficient is recomputed against the evidence sources.",
      "domainContext": "The evaluable predicate: the context (threshold, currency, market) this authority holds in. Criteria are evaluated against it."
    },
